Subject: [PATCH] populate-volatile: create TMP_FILE when there are no extra
 config files

With 00_core as the only file in /etc/default/volatiles, the loop that
concatenates the remaining config files never runs, so $TMP_FILE is never
created. check_requirements then fails on every boot with

  grep: /var/volatile/tmp/tmp_volatile.NNN: No such file or directory
  sed: /var/volatile/tmp/tmp_volatile.NNN: No such file or directory
  rm: can't remove '/var/volatile/tmp/tmp_volatile.NNN': No such file or directory

Create it empty instead of removing it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/populate-volatile.sh
+++ b/populate-volatile.sh
@@ -250,7 +250,9 @@
 	# faster to to concatenate them all together and process them once to
 	# avoid the overhead of calling check_requirements repeatedly
 	TMP_FILE="${TMPROOT}/tmp_volatile.$$"
-	rm -f "$TMP_FILE"
+	# The loop below appends nothing when 00_core is the only config file,
+	# and check_requirements would then read a file that does not exist.
+	: > "$TMP_FILE"
 
 	CFGFILES="$(ls -1 "${CFGDIR}" | grep -v "^${COREDEF}\$" | sort)"
 	for file in ${CFGFILES}; do
